@hostname = localhost
@port = 5124
@baseUrl = http://{{hostname}}:{{port}}/api

### =================================================================
### 1. AUTHENTICATION (LOGIN)
### =================================================================

# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "developer2026@example.com",
  "password": "SecurePassword123!"
}

#### Save the JWT token from the response automatically
@authToken = {{login.response.body.accessToken}}


### =================================================================
### 2. TAG ENDPOINTS (SECURED RESOURCES)
### =================================================================

### 2.1. Get all tags for the authenticated user
GET {{baseUrl}}/tags
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

### 2.2. Try to get tags without a token (Security Test - Must return 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tags
Accept: application/json

###

### 2.3. Create a new valid tag (Auto-sanitization in action)
# @name createTag
POST {{baseUrl}}/tags
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Tag Example   "
}

#### Save the newly created tag Id (converted to Guid in your API)
@createdTagId = {{createTag.response.body.id}}

###

### 2.4. Try to create an invalid tag (Validation Test - Must return 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tags
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": ""
}

###

### 2.5. Try to create a tag exceeding the character limit (Must return 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tags
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "This tag is ridiculously long and will definitely exceed the fifty character limit set in FluentValidation"
}

###

### 2.6. Delete the newly created tag using its Guid
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/tags/{{createdTagId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###

### 2.7. Try to delete a tag that no longer exists (Must return 404)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/tags/{{createdTagId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###

### 2.8. Try to delete a resource using an invalid Guid ID format (Must return 400 due to :guid constraint)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/tags/invalid-id-not-a-guid
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}